harmaceutical companies that may act as providers of NPD solutions.", "PROGRAMAS DE MEDICARE:Programas de Medicare are federal health insurance programs in the United States for individuals aged 65 and older or disabled, covering aspects of NED.", "PROGRAMAS DE MEDICAID:Programas de Medicaid are health insurance programs in the United States that provide coverage for low-income individuals, including aspects of NED.", "EE.UU.:EE.UU. is one of the eight countries mentioned that has limitations in data collection for epidemiological studies.", "BANS:BANS, which stands for the British Artificial Nutrition Survey, is a registry that focuses on estimating the prevalence of nutritional disorders in the UK. It has specifically published data regarding the prevalence of nutritional deficiencies (NED) and nutritional support (NPD). In 2011, BANS provided significant insights into the prevalence of NPD, contributing to the understanding of artificial nutrition needs within the British population.", "NADYA-SENPE:NADYA-SENPE is a specialized working group in Spain dedicated to home enteral nutrition. This group is responsible for maintaining various national registries that pertain to nutrition care, including annual registries of enteral and parenteral nutrition, which have been conducted since the late 1990s. Additionally, NADYA-SENPE is actively involved in research concerning health-related quality of life, particularly focusing on patients who receive home nutritional support. The group has also been collecting data on patients undergoing nutritional support therapy since 1992, specifically for those receiving NPD (Nutritional Parenteral Diet). Through these efforts, NADYA-SENPE plays a crucial role in advancing the understanding and management of nutritional care in Spain.", "NUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL DOMICILIARIA Y AMBULATORIA:The group of Artificial Nutrition Domiciliary and Ambulatory is involved in the study and registration of NED in Spain.", "BELGICA:", "OASIS:OASIS was a registry in the USA that recorded patients with NPD in 1987 before changing its name to the National Registry of Enteral and Parenteral Nutrition.", "SUSTAIN:SUSTAIN is A.S.P.E.N.'s National Patient Registry for Nutrition Care, specifically designed to focus on home parenteral nutrition outcomes. Established in 2011, SUSTAIN aims to include 100% of incident and prevalent patients with nutrition-related disorders (NPD). This comprehensive registry serves as a vital resource for tracking and improving the quality of nutrition care provided to patients receiving home parenteral nutrition.", "USA:The USA is a country where the OASIS registry was established to track patients with NPD.", "2014:The year 2014 is significant as it marks the last available data reporting 220 patients with NPD in the NADYA registry."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}